WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.135
Ron, Jesse, we're sending
you back to your home forges

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:05.804
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history--

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:09.275
[music playing]

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.513
--the Inigo
Montoya-inspired rapier.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.982
You know the guy. (SPANISH
ACCENT) You killed my father.

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.784
Prepare to-- forge, all right?

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.820
[chuckles]

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:26.125
Today we are pre-testing the
Inigo Montoya-inspired rapier.

00:00:26.191 --> 00:00:28.961
This is a version of
the Inigo Montoya rapier

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.063
that I love from
"Princess Bride."

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:33.366
So many people are
inspired by pop culture,

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:36.636
by seeing different blades and
different weapons from movies.

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:40.139
Now to actually see a version
of that, that's amazing.

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.107
Now, guess what, Doug?

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.441
You get to test it.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:43.510
Yes.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.044
WIL WILLIS (VOICEOVER):
Considered one

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.579
of the greatest swordsmen
of his generation,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.748
Inigo Montoya is a fictional
character from the cult classic

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:50.983
"The Princess Bride."

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.385
According to the story,
this famous blade

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.854
was the finest sword ever
crafted by his father.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.858
In parallel, Spanish swept hilt
rapiers of the 17th century,

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.293
featuring a diamond
cross-section

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.595
and a complex elaborate guard.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.532
Intended for dueling, rapiers
are lightweight and feature

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.634
a narrow point,
allowing for quick cuts

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.569
and deadly, accurate thrusts.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.338
One of the most recognized
sword fights in pop culture,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.340
Montoya infamously
uses the weapon

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.509
against his father's
killer, fulfilling

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.779
his quest for revenge.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.247
When you think
about the rapier

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.282
and how people wore
it in those days,

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.385
and thinking about
the movie, it inspires

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.487
you to try to move like them.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.792
One thing that I love about
this is the posture of the way

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.228
you wield the weapon.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.096
If it was like a dance--

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:40.500
the dance of balance,
the dance of posture--

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.135
and to be able to
move and to wield

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:45.838
one, but at the same time,
be like this very proud man

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:47.373
that Inigo Montoya was.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.879
The unique feel of the rapier
is that is a sword for dueling,

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:54.180
mostly for dueling one on one.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.882
So by having
something that light,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.818
and you pull it out, you should
be able to wield it nicely,

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:00.587
move around, not lose balance.

00:02:07.626 --> 00:02:09.295
Some weapons you see
out there, you can tell,

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.197
these are just
butchering weapons,

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.065
I mean, for mass
meleeing and fighting.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.867
But you can see also
that there's some weapons

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.301
that are created for finesse.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.204
Sometimes they say,
sometimes you're a butcher,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.506
sometimes you're a surgeon
where everything you do

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:24.310
is with a light touch, but just
as deadly as one that is very

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:26.246
wide in its chopping motions.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:33.218
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:34.787
We'll see you in four days.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.760 line:8%
JESSE (VOICEOVER): I'm about
to start building a Inigo

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.163
Montoya-inspired rapier.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.765
There's not a
whole lot of room

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.669
for error, so slow and steady
will be the name of the game.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.605
But I would really like to be
through with the blade today.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:55.274
The guard is very intricate,
and it's going to take

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:56.809
a lot of attention to detail.

00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:00.046
And the sooner I can get on
it, the better off I'll be.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.681
Here in a minute, we're
going to start getting

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.951
ready for the heat treat.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.720
I'm really worried
that a blade this long

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.790
is going to come out warped.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.559
This is the make
or break moment.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:15.395
So we're kind of
at a mystery place.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.129
We don't know whether
it's hard, and we don't

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.731
know whether it's straight.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:22.168
I noticed that there was just a
slight little yaw in the edge.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.371
Fixing to take all that
out in grinding today.

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.640
Next, I'm gonna
move on to the hilt.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.342
I'm planning on
forging all the parts

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.310
for the hilt out of
an old wagon wheel

00:03:31.376 --> 00:03:33.379
that my grandfather used to own.

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:35.247
I'm going to try to
make up a little time.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.883
I'm going to go ahead and
forge out a knuckle bow.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:42.988
And hopefully, by lunchtime, we
can start fabricating the hilt.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.391
This hilt's been
pretty demanding.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.726
There's about six
different pieces here.

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:50.596
We spent a lot of time trying
to make sure everything

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.098
was dialed in.

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:54.867
My hilt all came
together pretty nicely,

00:03:54.933 --> 00:03:56.168
just pulled it out of the etch.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.404
Everything looks good.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.373
My boys have popped
in to see us.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.608
MAN: Daddy, he's the one that's
taught us everything we know,

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:03.609
so.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.344
That-- you'll never
hear that again.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.947
That's the only time
they'll ever admit that.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:10.283 line:14%
[laughs]

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.185 line:14%
[iron clanking]

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.053
RON (VOICEOVER): I am
almost positive that they're

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.157
going to do some kind of a flex
test, so I'm choosing ADCRB2.

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.592
That should help with that.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.494
The hilt is one of the
more complex pieces here.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.596
I'm actually going to use
some really old wrought iron.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.298
RON (VOICEOVER):
One of the really

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.667
nice things about wrought
iron is that it's beautiful.

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.935
My plan is to acid
up so you can see

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.538
the lines around this thing.

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:34.973
I'm working on my normalization.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.275
This is make or break.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.778
If it works well, I'm all set.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:42.048
I grab hold of it with another
pair of tongs and go for it.

00:04:42.114 --> 00:04:45.585
I am very pleased right now to
have, at the end of day one,

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.020
a quench blade ready for temper.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.923
But my goal is to actually
get done with the blade today.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.893
It leaves me two days to work
on all of the embellishments.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.596
I may get into doing some
of the hilt work today.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.530
I want to see how it
goes with the grinding.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:02.501
If I overgrind, I could
completely destroy the blade.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.304
There's a reason that it
took Inigo Montoya's father

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:06.639
a year to make this sword.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.807
There are so many
pieces to this.

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:11.878
Now I can focus on getting
that really complex

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.846
handle and hilt all together.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.514
I'm forging out these
bigger rings that

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.516
are on the side of the hand.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.984
That's eventually
going to become

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:21.420
this really complex basket.

00:05:21.486 --> 00:05:23.489
Not perfect, but for
day four, I'll take it.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.324
Regardless of the
outcome on this thing,

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:26.859
I've had a blast making this.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.962
Win, lose or draw, it's
just been so much fun.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:30.963
Good job.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.565
Thank you.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:35.034
All right, Daddy Bladesmiths.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.769
My name Douglas Mercaida.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.571
I will kill the dummies.

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:39.838
They are prepared to die.

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.074
[chuckling]

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.408
To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.743
your weapons will do, I
will take your rapiers

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.244
and deliver some
thrust and slashes

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.579
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.180
Ron, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.181
Absolutely.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:50.148
Let's do it.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.419
[music playing]

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:30.523
All right, Ron.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.458
Let's talk about
your rapier here.

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.794
It is a little bit
on the heavier side,

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:35.895
but it's wieldable.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:40.299
And with a nice swish of
a slash, it cuts deeply.

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.501
Overall, sir, your
rapier, it will kill.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.070
Good job.
- Thank you.

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:45.304
All right, Jesse.
It's your turn.

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.305
You ready, sir?

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:48.073
Yes, sir.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:51.811
[music playing]

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.201
All right, Jesse.

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:17.502
Let's talk about
your blade here.

00:07:17.569 --> 00:07:19.438
It's about the same weight.

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:21.340
The thrust penetrate
all the way,

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:24.376
and to slash, well, deep cuts.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:27.079
Overall, sir, your
blade will kill.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.080
Thank you, sir.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.215
That's what I came to hear.

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:33.185
DAVID BAKER: All
right, gentlemen.

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:34.487
It's time for the strength test.

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:37.289
And yes, I am going to
torture your blades.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.957
Ron, you're up first.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:41.594
All right.

00:07:41.694 --> 00:07:43.095
[thump]

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.239
If you haven't guessed
already, it's a flex test.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:57.877
[music playing]

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.901
Good job.

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.669
Good job.

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:24.770
OK, Ron.

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:27.739
That's a brutal test,
and he did really well.

00:08:27.806 --> 00:08:29.609
If you look at
your blade, there's

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:34.413
the slightest of bend in one
direction, barely noticeable.

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:37.950
The dimensions of the
guard are spot on.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.051
And it's definitely
a strong blade.

00:08:40.118 --> 00:08:41.087
Nicely done.

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:42.154
Thank you very much.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.255
Jesse, you ready for this?

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:44.790
'Bout as nervous
as a long-tailed

00:08:44.856 --> 00:08:47.092
cat in a room full of
rocking chairs, but go ahead.

00:08:47.159 --> 00:08:49.128
[laughs]

00:08:50.496 --> 00:08:54.667
[music playing]

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:17.623
[exhales]

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:21.160
First things, Jesse, the
guards in the proper scale--

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.627
really nicely done.

00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:25.731
Issue is, you picked
up a bit of a bend.

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:28.534
Still completely
functional, usable blade.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:29.535
Well done.

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:30.836
Thank you.

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:35.507
Bladesmiths, this
is the sharpness test.

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:37.276
This is all about how
sharp your blade is

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:39.812
and what it does to this dummy.

00:09:39.878 --> 00:09:41.346
Ron, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:09:41.413 --> 00:09:42.348
Yes, sir.

00:09:42.415 --> 00:09:44.883
Let's do this.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:49.355
[cracking]

00:09:56.963 --> 00:09:57.763
All right, Ron.

00:09:57.829 --> 00:09:59.265
Let's talk about your edge here.

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:02.901
This cut through the clothing
and right into the foam.

00:10:03.001 --> 00:10:05.237
And of course when
thrusting, it goes deep.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:07.940
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:09.208
- Thank you.
- All right, Jesse.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:10.509
It's your turn, sir.
You ready?

00:10:10.576 --> 00:10:11.510
Yes, sir.

00:10:11.577 --> 00:10:14.246
Let's do this.

00:10:14.313 --> 00:10:17.817
[cracking]

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:28.227
All right, Jesse.

00:10:28.294 --> 00:10:30.462
I can still see the little
bend it took at the tip.

00:10:30.528 --> 00:10:33.232
But the edges are razor sharp.

00:10:33.332 --> 00:10:35.267
On the thrust, it goes deep.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:37.069
It will cut.
- Thank you, sir.

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.237
[music playing]

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:40.472
Ron, Jesse, you
guys have turned

00:10:40.538 --> 00:10:42.808
in some really quality blades.

00:10:42.874 --> 00:10:44.943
This is a difficult
decision for us to make.

00:10:45.043 --> 00:10:52.484
And our Forged in
Fire champion is Ron.

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:53.785
Congratulations.

00:10:53.852 --> 00:10:55.821
You are the new Forged
in Fire champion.

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:58.090
Jesse, please
surrender your blade.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.825
JESSE: Not being
the "Forged in Fire"

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:02.394
champion is kind of-- it's
not what I was looking for.

00:11:02.461 --> 00:11:04.162
But if I made this
blade again, I

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:06.198
would have took a little
more time on my heat treat,

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:07.733
made sure I had it perfect.

00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:09.435
Ron, congratulations.

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.136
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:13.605
You've led your family
to this position,

00:11:13.705 --> 00:11:16.841
and you'll be taking
home a check for $10,000.

00:11:16.908 --> 00:11:18.243
Good job, brother.
- Thank you.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.211
[applause]

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:20.779
It feels spectacular.

00:11:20.879 --> 00:11:23.048
From beginning to end, this
has been a great experience.

00:11:23.114 --> 00:11:25.383
So the Hardman house
is getting the "Forged

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.187
in Fire" Championship.

